Lua 5.3.6 (https://www.lua.org, MIT licence) as bundled with Lua Telemetry.

This copy is used to pre-compile the Lua Telemetry scripts into bytecode that
loads on EdgeTX 2.11 and later (including EdgeTX 3.x), which run Lua 5.3.
OpenTX and EdgeTX up to 2.10 run Lua 5.2 and use ../lua-5.2.4 instead.

Local changes compared to the upstream 5.3.6 sources:

* src/ldump.c and src/lundump.c: the bytecode header stores/checks a 4-byte
  "size_t" field instead of the host size_t, exactly as EdgeTX does, so that
  bytecode produced on a 64-bit host loads on the radio.
* src/luac.c: minimal replacement for the official luac (only "-s" and "-o"
  are supported).
* src/Makefile: builds with -DLUA_32BITS -DLUA_COMPAT_5_2 -DLUA_FLOORN2I=1,
  the configuration used by the EdgeTX firmware.
